{"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Integrating with test frameworks","modules":[{"name":"SnapshotTesting"}],"role":"article"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The Apple ecosystem currently has two primary testing frameworks, and unfortunately they are not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"compatible with each other. There is the XCTest framework, which is a private framework provided","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"by Apple and heavily integrated into Xcode. And now there is Swift Testing, an open source testing","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"framework built in Swift that is capable of integrating into a variety of environments.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"These two frameworks are not compatible in the sense that an assertion made in one framework","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"from a test in the other framework will not trigger a test failure. So, if you are writing a test"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with the new "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Test"},{"type":"text","text":" macro style, and you use a test helper that ultimately calls "},{"code":"XCTFail","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" under"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the hood, that will not bubble up to an actual test failure when tests are run. And similarly, if"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"you have a test case inheriting from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"XCTestCase"},{"type":"text","text":" that ultimiately invokes the new style "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"#expect"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"macro, that too will not actually trigger a test failure.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"However, these details have all been hidden away in the SnapshotTesting library. You can simply"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"use "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/assertSnapshot(of:as:named:options:fileID:file:testName:line:column:)"},{"type":"text","text":" in either an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"XCTestCase"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"subclass ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"or"}]},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Test"},{"type":"text","text":", and it will dynamically detect what context it is running in and trigger"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the correct test failure:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["@Test ","func testFeature() {","  assertSnapshot(of: MyView(), as: .image)  \/\/ ✅","}","","class FeatureTests: XCTestCase {","  func testFeature() {","    assertSnapshot(of: MyView(), as: .image)  \/\/ ✅","  }","}"]},{"text":"Configuring snapshots","anchor":"Configuring-snapshots","type":"heading","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For the most part, asserting on snapshots works the same whether you are using XCTest or Swift"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Testing. There is one major difference, and that is how snapshot configuration works. There are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"two major ways snapshots can be configured: "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/SnapshotTestingConfiguration\/diffTool-swift.property"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/SnapshotTestingConfiguration\/record-swift.property","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"code":"diffTool","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" property allows you to customize how a command is printed to the test failure"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"message that allows you to quickly open a diff of two files, such as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"http:\/\/kaleidoscope.app","isActive":true},{"text":". The ","type":"text"},{"code":"record","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" property allows you to change the mode of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"assertion so that new snapshots are generated and saved to disk.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"These properties can be overridden for a scope of an operation using the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/withSnapshotTesting(record:diffTool:snapshotNaming:referenceStorage:locale:timeZone:calendar:operation:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"function. In a Swift Testing context"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"you can apply the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/Testing\/Trait\/snapshots","type":"reference"},{"text":" trait to either a single test or an entire suite:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import SnapshotTesting","","@Suite(.snapshots(record: .failed, diffTool: .ksdiff))","struct FeatureTests {","  …","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This will override the "},{"code":"diffTool","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"record","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" properties for each test in the suite."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"In an XCTest context, the simplest way to do this is to override the ","type":"text"},{"code":"invokeTest","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" method on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"XCTestCase"},{"type":"text","text":" and wrap it in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withSnapshotTesting"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["class FeatureTests: XCTestCase {","  override func invokeTest() {","    withSnapshotTesting(record: .failed, diffTool: .ksdiff) {","      super.invokeTest()","    }","  }","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This will override the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"diffTool"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"record"},{"text":" properties for each test function.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"UI-Testing","text":"UI Testing","type":"heading","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Xcode’s UI testing tools are currently incompatible with Swift Testing. Simply adding"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Testing"},{"text":" to any UI test target file will cause a compilation error saying that “Testing”","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"cannot be found. This complicates using SnapshotTesting in UI test targets because it needs to"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"import Testing in order to provide the test helpers mentioned above.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The way in which Xcode disallows importing Testing in UI test targets is via the presence of a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"special Swift flag:"}]},{"syntax":null,"code":["-module_alias Testing=_Testing_Unavailable"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This is done so that people do not expect "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"#expect"},{"text":" and other Testing tools to work in UI test","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"targets. If you want to use SnapshotTesting in a UI test target, we recommend that you remove","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"this flag:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Open your project’s settings and navigate to the settings for your UI testing target.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Search for “Other Swift flags” in the “Build Settings” tab."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Delete the ","type":"text"},{"code":"$(inherited)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" flag.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Now you can ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import SnapshotTesting"},{"type":"text","text":" in UI test targets "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"and","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" make use of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"assertSnapshot"},{"type":"text","text":". But"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"do remember that you "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"cannot"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" use "},{"code":"#expect","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or any of the other tools from Swift Testing.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/IntegratingWithTestFrameworks"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/snapshottesting\/integratingwithtestframeworks"]}],"kind":"article","seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/assertSnapshot(of:as:named:options:fileID:file:testName:line:column:)","doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/SnapshotAssertionOptions","doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/MigrationGuides"],"anchor":"Essentials","generated":true,"title":"Essentials"}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"pat